      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2022-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We can simplify this expression as follows:\n\n\\[\\begin{aligned} 3 +& \\dfrac{1}{3 + \\dfrac{1}{3 + \\dfrac{1}{3}}} \\\\ &= 3 + \\dfrac{1}{3 + \\dfrac{1}{\\dfrac{10}{3}}} \\\\ &= 3 + \\dfrac{1}{3 + \\dfrac{3}{10}} \\\\ &= 3 + \\dfrac{1}{\\dfrac{33}{10}} \\\\ &= 3 + \\dfrac{10}{33} \\\\ &= \\dfrac{109}{33}. \\end{aligned}\\]\n\nThus, D is the correct answer.",
